%N A252653 Number of free polyominoes with n cells containing a complete self-avoiding walk.
%C A252653 A Hamiltonian path visits every vertex exactly once; its endpoints are unrestricted. Holes are allowed. A shape with several paths still contributes one, and paths, orientations, rootings and endpoint choices are not counted separately. - _Carlo Corti_, Nov 04 2026
%H A252653 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23953385">Exact Enumeration of Free Polyominoes Admitting a Hamiltonian Path through 22 Cells</a>, Zenodo archive, 2026.
%H A252653 Ernest French, <a href="https://fuseki.net/polycover/index.html">Covering Free Polyominos</a>
%H A252653 pursekeeper.dev, <a href="https://pursekeeper.dev/verified/03-A252653-rook-walk-coverable-polyominoes">Six further terms of OEIS A252653 (rook-walk-coverable polyominoes)</a>, pursekeeper claims pilot, claim 3, 2026.
%F A252653 From _Carlo Corti_, Nov 04 2026: (Start)
%F A252653 A283162(n) <= a(n) <= A000105(n) for n >= 1.
%F A252653 a(2*n) <= A056785(n) = A000105(2*n) - A213376(n) for n >= 1.
%F A252653 A361288(n) <= a(2*n) for n >= 2. (End)
%Y A252653 Cf. A000105, A056785, A213376, A283162, A361288.
